    "narrative": "Our offensive engine for May 8th is anchored by **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Bryson Stott** (70.70), both of whom present the highest ceilings on the board. **Taylor Ward** draws a premier matchup against Lopez, benefitting from a significant park factor boost and favorable platoon splits that push his efficiency into elite territory. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** remains a high-priority start due to a rare confluence of a hitter-friendly environment and a \"slow-to-the-plate\" opposing starter in Dollander, which dramatically elevates his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical lever in our scoring model. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** continues to be a mandatory start despite facing the southpaw Prielipp, as his raw power and order placement render him matchup-proof, maintaining a strong 68.14 score.\n\nThe decision to bench **Masyn Winn** (51.12) was the most difficult call of the morning; while he projects as a serviceable option, his efficiency profile was ultimately nudged out by the platoon and wind-assisted upside of players like **Matt Chapman** and **Luis Arraez**. Those two, along with **Jung Hoo Lee**, should see a measurable bump in output today given the favorable wind conditions currently forecasted. Conversely, we must maintain caution with **Will Smith**, whose score of 44.75 is heavily suppressed by a grueling matchup against Chris Sale. While **Will Smith** remains in the lineup for now, his output is highly volatile today, and he remains the most susceptible to a late-inning replacement should his efficiency metrics drop further once official lineups are finalized. \n\nBeyond these tactical alignments, we are monitoring several risk factors. **Lawrence Butler** carries a high park-factor projection, yet his score is tempered significantly by an underlying struggle against Bradish. Similarly, **Wenceel Perez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** are currently operating on \"Lineup Pending\" status; if either player falls out of the top six in their respective orders, their value will diminish rapidly. We are intentionally holding **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Jonathan Aranda** on the bench today, as their projected outputs do not sufficiently overcome the scarcity of our target categories compared to the daily consistency offered by **Brendan Donovan** and **Cal Raleigh**.",
